+## Engine audit for NewBike-Balance-v1 (2026-09-13) — sim-side problems
+
+Found against the run's logged params/env.yaml (2026-09-11_01-38-54), the USD
+payloads (Physics/physics.usda, physx.usda, materials.usda), bicycle_cfg.py and
+newbike_balance_env_cfg.py:
+
+1. solver_position/velocity_iteration_count = 4/2 (NEW_BIKE_BASE_CFG spawn
+   articulation_props) — the ROOT CAUSE of the ~x24.5 sluggish drive: the TGS
+   under-delivers the effort-actuated wheel per step. Probe-verified: 16/8
+   restores the rigid response (the wheel slams the 61.6 rad/s limit).
+2. enable_external_forces_every_iteration = False (env.yaml sim.physics) —
+   CONFIRMED 2026-09-13 (in-air welded-root probe, /tmp/sim_extforce_probe.py):
+   the PRIMARY cause of the sluggish drive. At 4/2 + False the wheel plateaus
+   at 23.11 rad/s (a1>=0.6); flipping the flag True at the SAME 4/2 restores
+   the rigid physics (61.60 rad/s = the velocity limit; effort follows the
+   authored tau = 6.28*a1 - 0.05*w exactly, incl. 0.00 Nm at a1=0.2). The
+   16/8 iteration fix and the flag flip are two independent repairs of the
+   same truncation: the once-per-step force injection + 2 sweeps cannot
+   propagate the impulse. The fall-probe log's "may cause noisy velocities"
+   warning names exactly this.
+3. Runtime mass ~+20% above the USD payload masses — the collision geometry
+   contributes default-density mass (the USD colliders declare no density;
+   measured in the inertia probe). The MuJoCo model carries only the payload
+   masses (2.3996 kg total). Un-compensated.
+4. DR active in this run on every reset: randomize_mass 0.5-1.5x,
+   randomize_com, tire friction U(0.5, 1.2) (num_buckets 32),
+   randomize_actuator_gains 0.9-1.1x. play_eval numbers are DR-averaged;
+   any nominal-only comparison (e.g. the MuJoCo deploy) must use the nominal
+   envelope, not the eval mean.
+5. Reset state: the initial_state event resets root z=0, roll U(-0.1, 0.1)
+   rad, roll rate U(-0.25, 0.25) rad/s every episode — NOT the fixed zeros
+   the MuJoCo env comment assumes (that was 0950's protocol).
+6. Friction reference values: ground pinned 1.0 (startup event); tire = the
+   global physxMaterial 0.5/0.5 isotropic (the USD has no per-wheel physics
+   material — materials.usda carries only the visual "silver"). The MuJoCo
+   wheels now carry the sim's pair: sliding 0.75 (MuJoCo combines pair
+   friction by MAX — verified empirically; MuJoCo's triple is
+   sliding/torsional/rolling — the earlier 'anisotropic 1.0/0.005'
+   phrasing misread the orange-bike triple).
+7. Sim-side quirk: balance_wheel_net_termination reads with a one-step lag
+   (its own docstring); the MuJoCo env checks immediately. Immaterial.
+8. physx.usda sets maxJointVelocity 100 rad/s (5729.578 deg/s) on the
+   steering joint — dominated by the actuator's velocity_limit_sim 23.9;
+   no effect.
+9. GPU patch-based friction (friction_offset_threshold 0.04,
+   friction_correlation_distance 0.025) has no MuJoCo analog — model-level
+   difference, no config translation.
